            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0000\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000\", \"F025:F026\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Paragraph (a) establishes the railroad crossing stopping requirement with the explicit caveat 'Except as provided in paragraph (b) of this section', while paragraph (b)(1) provides that a stop need not be made at streetcar crossings or industrial switching tracks in a business district. Adding an explicit exception qualification edge from C0009 targeting C0000 accurately captures this governing caveat.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000\", \"F025\", \"F027\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Paragraph (a) conditions the mandatory stop on the exceptions in paragraph (b), and paragraph (b)(2) provides that a stop need not be made when a police officer or crossing flagman directs traffic to proceed. Adding an exception edge from C0010 qualifying C0000 faithfully converts the prose caveat into an explicit qualification.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0002\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000\", \"F025\", \"F028\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Paragraph (a) explicitly subordinates the grade crossing stop requirement to paragraph (b), and paragraph (b)(3) exempts stopping when a functioning highway traffic signal transmits a green indication permitting passage without stopping under local law. Creating an exception edge from C0011 targeting C0000 is directly supported by the text.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0003\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000\", \"F025\", \"F029\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Paragraph (a) states the stop requirement subject to paragraph (b), and paragraph (b)(4) specifies that a stop need not be made at marked abandoned railroad grade crossings. Linking C0012 to C0000 as an exception edge correctly reflects this statutory qualification.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0004\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000\", \"F025\", \"F030\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Paragraph (a) introduces the stopping duty subject to paragraph (b), and paragraph (b)(5) provides that a stop need not be made at industrial or spur line crossings marked 'Exempt'. Connecting C0013 as an exception qualifying C0000 accurately captures this relationship without altering modal force or scope.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
